# Legacy Drupal webform export — PERSONAL DATA, NEVER COMMITTED
#
# Base64 exports of the legacy site's webform_submission rows, pulled locally
# for the one-time registration import (register_public / register_inhouse).
# They carry REAL CUSTOMER DATA in the clear once decoded: names, email
# addresses, phone numbers and tax IDs.
#
# They are working files for a migration that runs twice — a bulk pass and a
# catch-up on cutover night — and then never again. Nothing in the application
# reads them, so there is no version of this repo that needs them, and the only
# thing committing them could achieve is putting customer PII in every clone and
# every fork of the history permanently.
#
# The three OTHER files in docs/legacy/ stay tracked, deliberately:
# legacy-courses.json, course-match-report.tsv and course-match-map.json are
# course titles, ids and submission COUNTS — no personal data in any of them.
docs/legacy/*.b64
